WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.061 --> 00:00:09.209
When Dr. Mead finally arrived from New York, Dr. Warren drove him to the Harrington house.

2
00:00:09.210 --> 00:00:14.398
Aunt Polly introduced the specialist to Pollyanna and Miss Hunt, the nurse.

3
00:00:14.399 --> 00:00:19.765
"I like you, Dr. Mead!" Pollyanna said after he examined her.

4
00:00:19.766 --> 00:00:23.968
"Maybe it's because you look a lot like my doctor."

5
00:00:23.969 --> 00:00:31.495
" Your doctor?" Dr. Mead looked at Dr. Warren, who was talking to the

6
00:00:31.496 --> 00:00:35.934
nurse. Dr. Warren was a small man with a brown

7
00:00:35.935 --> 00:00:39.661
beard. Dr. Mead was a tall man with a cheerful

8
00:00:39.662 --> 00:00:43.079
smile. "But we don't look anything

9
00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:49.409
alike!" Pollyanna glanced at Dr. Warren. "Oh, he isn't my

10
00:00:49.410 --> 00:00:55.881
doctor. Dr. Warren is Aunt Polly's doctor. My doctor is Dr.

11
00:00:55.882 --> 00:01:00.258
Chilton." At the mention of Dr. Chilton, Aunt Polly turned red.

12
00:01:00.259 --> 00:01:05.986
"You see, I wanted Dr. Chilton right from the beginning," Pollyanna went on.

13
00:01:05.987 --> 00:01:08.495
"But Aunt Polly wanted you.

14
00:01:08.496 --> 00:01:13.170
She said you knew more than Dr. Chilton did about broken legs like mine.

15
00:01:13.171 --> 00:01:19.050
Of course, if you do, then I'll be glad about that. So, do you?"

16
00:01:19.051 --> 00:01:23.654
"Only time will tell, young lady," Dr. Mead said gently.

17
00:01:23.655 --> 00:01:28.279
His smile had disappeared, and he looked quite serious.

18
00:01:28.280 --> 00:01:35.234
"Now, if everyone else could join me in the hall, I'd like to speak to you."

19
00:01:35.235 --> 00:01:39.377
What happened next upset everyone in the house.

20
00:01:39.378 --> 00:01:44.484
As the adults talked in the hall, Fluffy, the cat, poked at Pollyanna's door.

21
00:01:44.485 --> 00:01:48.134
If the door had been closed, she would not have succeeded.

22
00:01:48.135 --> 00:01:54.012
But Fluffy managed to use her nose and paw to push the door until it stood ajar.

23
00:01:54.013 --> 00:02:00.239
The cat jumped onto the bed, just as Aunt Polly gave an anguished cry.

24
00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:06.556
"Not that! Oh, Dr. Mead, anything but that. You don't mean . . ."

25
00:02:06.557 --> 00:02:10.472
Aunt Polly had to force herself to say the awful words.

26
00:02:10.473 --> 00:02:14.830
"You don't mean she'll never walk again

27
00:02:14.831 --> 00:02:23.964
!" From the bedroom Pollyanna cried out in terror. "Aunt Polly! Aunt

28
00:02:23.965 --> 00:02:32.099
Polly!" Seeing the open door and realizing Pollyanna had overheard, Aunt Polly gave a low

29
00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:36.088
moan. Then, for the first time in her life, she

30
00:02:36.089 --> 00:02:40.477
fainted. Fortunately, Dr. Mead caught her before she hit the floor.

31
00:02:40.478 --> 00:02:49.537
"I'm coming, Pollyanna!" Miss Hunt stumbled toward the open door while the two doctors tended to Aunt Polly.

32
00:02:49.538 --> 00:02:55.709
In Pollyanna's room Fluffy was vainly trying to attract the panicked child's attention.

33
00:02:55.710 --> 00:03:02.329
"Miss Hunt, please, I want Aunt Polly." Pollyanna's eyes were wide with fear.

34
00:03:02.330 --> 00:03:07.561
"I want her right now. Quick, please get her for me!"

35
00:03:07.562 --> 00:03:10.635
The nurse closed the door and hurried over to the bed.

36
00:03:10.636 --> 00:03:14.851
"She can't come just this minute, dear. She will come a little later.

37
00:03:14.852 --> 00:03:18.608
What do you want? Is there something I can get for you?"

38
00:03:18.609 --> 00:03:23.863
Pollyanna shook her head. "I want to know more about what she just said.

39
00:03:23.864 --> 00:03:31.119
Did you hear her? I want Aunt Polly. She said something, and I need her to tell me it isn't true."

40
00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:34.819
Miss Hunt tried to speak but couldn't find the right words.

41
00:03:34.820 --> 00:03:39.012
Something in the nurse's face added to Pollyanna's terror.

42
00:03:39.013 --> 00:03:47.921
"Miss Hunt, you did hear her! It is true! You mean, I'll never walk again?"

43
00:03:47.922 --> 00:03:53.002
"There, there, dear, don't—" The nurse choked back her own tears.

44
00:03:53.003 --> 00:03:56.023
"Maybe Dr. Mead didn't know what he was saying.

45
00:03:56.024 --> 00:04:01.212
Perhaps he was mistaken. Lots of things could happen."

46
00:04:01.213 --> 00:04:07.804
"But Aunt Polly said he knew more than anybody else about broken legs like mine!"

47
00:04:07.805 --> 00:04:12.585
"Yes, I know, but all doctors make mistakes sometimes.

48
00:04:12.586 --> 00:04:17.033
Don't think anything more about it right now." Pollyanna

49
00:04:17.034 --> 00:04:25.538
flung out her arms. "But I can't help thinking about it," she sobbed. "It's

50
00:04:25.539 --> 00:04:32.508
all I can think about. How will I go to school or visit my friends? If

51
00:04:32.509 --> 00:04:38.665
I can't walk, how will I ever be glad about anything ?"

52
00:04:38.666 --> 00:04:43.898
While Pollyanna sobbed, Miss Hunt had been preparing some medicine.

53
00:04:43.899 --> 00:04:53.102
"Just take this, dear," she said. "Maybe after you rest, things will seem brighter."

54
00:04:53.103 --> 00:04:57.318
Pollyanna took the medicine and sipped the water offered by Miss Hunt.

55
00:04:57.319 --> 00:05:00.558
"That sounds like something Father used to say.

56
00:05:00.559 --> 00:05:04.933
But he'd never been told he wouldn't walk again.

57
00:05:04.934 --> 00:05:09.507
Nothing could be worse than that, could it?"

58
00:05:09.508 --> 00:05:15.229
Miss Hunt had no answer for Pollyanna's question.

